### Quantities with a unit.
###
### The viewer formats the number (its precision is a measurement matter) and
### hands it over as `{ $value }`; the unit's symbol and where it sits are the
### catalog's. A bare symbol is the unit on its own, as the stats card's Unit row
### shows it.

## File sizes, in the binary steps file managers use

ui-units-bytes-value = { $value } B
ui-units-kilobytes-value = { $value } KB
ui-units-megabytes-value = { $value } MB
ui-units-gigabytes-value = { $value } GB

## Lengths, in the units a DCC authors in

ui-units-meters = m
ui-units-meters-value = { $value } m
ui-units-centimeters = cm
ui-units-centimeters-value = { $value } cm
ui-units-millimeters = mm
ui-units-millimeters-value = { $value } mm
ui-units-inches = in
ui-units-inches-value = { $value } in
ui-units-feet = ft
ui-units-feet-value = { $value } ft
ui-units-yards = yd
ui-units-yards-value = { $value } yd
